From f8aa219b60bc87b260156eea7c8468a18861b917 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:39:51 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] libblkid: add AMD RAIDXpert2 (RAIDCore) RAID member prober

AMD RAIDXpert2 is the RAID of AMD chipsets (X399, X570, X670, X870...).
Its BIOS and drivers write a label at LBA 0x5000 of every disk they
initialize: "RAIDCore" at offset 8, a version (0x30000), the location
of the configuration ring, and a 64-bit checksum over the rest of the
sector.  Without a prober these disks look like disks with an MBR and
one partition of type 0x82, so nothing warns before they are reused.

Report them as amd_raid_member when the version and the checksum match.

The test image is the first 12 MiB of a member of a RAID10 created by
the BIOS of an ASUS X399 board, rebuilt from a public CC0 dump
(https://github.com/PlaidPiper/x399-raidcore-fixtures); no volume data
is included.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.
